00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:34.910
<i>Because we fall in love, there's sadness</i>

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:36.950
<i>Yeah, come on!</i>

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:39.250
<i>You gonna feel so</i>

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:41.250
<i>Yeah, come on!</i>

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:49.660
Chapter 11 Plot

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:01.150
That should be enough patrolling.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:03.430
Please go on back without me.

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:04.380
Yes, sir.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.410
Cinnamon Cookies

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:12.290
Five Color Peas

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:13.660
Good Fortune Twists

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:16.110
Soy Candy Sticks

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:30.660
Excuse me, please give me
two bags of this hard candy!

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:46.040
Guess we'll take this too.

00:02:56.450 --> 00:02:58.120
This is no good.

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.950
Tetsu, quit playing around
and help me out, will you?

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:03.960
I don't know what I should do.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.830
Go air these out or something.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:16.270
All of these too.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.510
Okay, okay.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:29.640
Hi there, Tetsu. Working hard, I see.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:32.680
Mr. Okita! Are you on patrol?

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:41.160
Paw.

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:53.700
It's a secret, okay?

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:54.330
Yes, sir!

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:11.620
Ow, ow, ow...

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.790
Sorry about that, I
wasn't paying attention.

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:19.940
Not at all! I was careless as well.

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:23.160
What's the matter?

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:25.200
Is there something weighing on your mind?

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.070
No...

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:29.370
No, it's nothing.

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:31.240
It's just that my eyes are bad.

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:39.840
Mr. Yamanami...

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:47.090
My stomach...

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:52.910
Hey, man. Hey, man, ya dropped
this book, didn't ya? I got it for ya.

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:55.560
Thank you very...

00:04:58.950 --> 00:05:00.900
Wait, wait, wait, I say!

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:03.080
Please let go of me!

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:06.860
You drop a book on my head and
you've got nothin' to say to me?!

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.500
Head?!

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:11.490
What else does it look like 'cept a head?

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:15.210
You're that... strange...

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:19.080
The mystery nice men.

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:22.200
That would be "nice guy."

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:24.720
Oh-ho, ya know yer English.

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:28.450
What are you doing here?

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:33.040
What am I doin'? Come to visit, of course.

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:34.020
Excuse me?

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:35.910
Visit whom?

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:39.420
The Peacemaker's son, who else?

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:45.830
But the more I look at ya, the more
I see you're a spittin' image.

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:48.860
If ya just had a goatee, it'd be perfect.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:53.410
You're the Peacemaker's son, aren't you?

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:57.460
Why do you know that?

00:05:57.830 --> 00:06:01.620
Well, it'd been buggin' me
since I met ya in Hyogo,

00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:03.300
so I did a little checkin' up on ya.

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:08.700
The man was relatively
well known in the underground.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:13.850
Haven't ya ever been dragged into
some mess 'cause of that face?

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:20.950
Still, to think the Peacemaker's
son joined the Shinsengumi...

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:23.040
Talk about the world
bein' full of surprises.

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:25.200
Please stop this!

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:28.780
My mother and father
both died two years ago.

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:32.660
I have no intention of
answering any of your questions.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:33.950
Please leave me alone.

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:36.450
Now, now, don't get so cross.

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:41.250
I've no plans to pry into you
and your brother's lives, so relax.

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:46.290
Tatsunosuke and Tetsunosuke Ichimura,

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:49.660
you guys aren't like the people here.

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:51.140
Come with me.

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:54.140
Let's go washin' Japan together!

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:03.690
<i>I can't let Tetsu come
into contact with this man.</i>

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:08.900
Please go home.

00:07:09.700 --> 00:07:12.660
The Shogunate... The world... Even Japan...

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:14.910
It's none of my business
what happens to them.

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:19.660
Totally opposite words
comin' outta the same face.

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:22.240
Makes me sad.

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:28.130
Listen to me. Keep it a
secret that ya saw me.

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:32.750
Oh, Tatsunosuke.

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:36.200
Are you finished with your rounds?
Thank you for your hard work.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:39.910
And thank you for your hard work
sorting documents, Tatsunosuke.

00:07:39.910 --> 00:07:44.620
But this certainly is an odd place
to bump into each other, Ryoma.

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:52.030
Oh, Okki! Long time no see!
You're as cute as ever, I see!

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:56.490
I have no clue what you're
saying, the same as ever!

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:12.510
Your greetings are as violent as ever.

00:08:12.950 --> 00:08:19.220
Yes. Unfortunately, I am currently on duty,
so I cannot overlook this and let you go.

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:39.240
To think that Mr. Wanted Ryoma would visit
Shinsengumi Headquarters of his own will.

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:43.950
Did you find someone again that
you want to scout, as you say?

00:08:43.950 --> 00:08:49.120
Hey, man, I'm still scoutin'
you too, of course, Okki.

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:52.710
But I've found 'bout two
new ones that I want.

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:57.510
This place sure is a
treasure trove of nice talent.

00:08:57.950 --> 00:09:01.080
Really? I'm glad to hear that.

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:02.470
Well, then, Ryoma...

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:06.350
Please have a good long
look around from your cell.

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:07.700
All right!

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:09.480
I'll have to say "no thank you" to that!

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:33.500
Don't let him get away!

00:09:33.500 --> 00:09:35.630
All members, completely
surround headquarters!

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:38.430
Do not be daunted by his gun! Capture him!

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:47.520
Hey! Dragon-boy!

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:50.910
It's goodbye for today.

00:09:50.910 --> 00:09:54.440
I'll come again, so say
hi to Iron-boy for me!

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:58.330
I'm the Japanese Ryoma Sakamoto!

00:09:58.330 --> 00:10:01.620
The man who'll someday be
the Peacemaker of Japan!

00:10:02.250 --> 00:10:05.040
You people'd better watch out!

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:07.370
Someday, Japan will be reborn!

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:08.750
Whether you like it or not!

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:23.680
Mr. Okita, who in the world was that?

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:27.250
Oh? You're not acquaintances?

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:28.270
No.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.270
Ryoma Sakamoto, a ronin from Tosa.

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:37.790
He is a master of the
Hokushin Single-Sword Style

00:10:37.790 --> 00:10:40.830
and a man who once served
as head teacher at Kochiba,

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:45.290
but he deserted his clan and has quite
a few dealings with the loyalists as well.

00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:49.120
In other words, a dangerous
man of consequence.

00:10:50.500 --> 00:10:53.460
Other than that, about all we know

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:57.660
is that he's a <i>very </i>funny person, I guess.

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:15.480
Tatsu!

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:17.910
Tatsu...

00:11:17.910 --> 00:11:19.330
Did something happen?!

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:21.200
I just heard a really loud noise.

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:25.450
Yeah, this wanted man
came in earlier and...

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:26.370
He ran away already.

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:31.210
Pardon me...

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:34.040
Which way to the kitchen?

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:49.560
Ayu!

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:53.450
Miss Hotaru's here as hired help.

00:11:53.450 --> 00:11:55.830
Oh, you saw the flier?

00:11:55.830 --> 00:11:56.310
Yes, ma'am.

00:11:56.870 --> 00:12:00.330
Don't be so stiff and formal. Relax.

00:12:00.330 --> 00:12:02.450
I was so scared!

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:06.830
The gentlemen had their swords drawn.

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:10.000
And I almost bumped into them...

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:12.410
Now, now, don't cry so.

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:14.160
After all, this <i>is </i>the Shinsengumi.

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:17.460
You won't be able to work if you
keep jumping at things like that.

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:21.540
Or would you rather not?

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:24.970
No, I look forward to working with you!

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:28.640
Masuya

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:31.140
Hey, Hotaru!

00:12:31.910 --> 00:12:34.870
Hotaru is at Mibu starting today.

00:12:36.500 --> 00:12:37.900
Had you forgotten?

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:43.740
Mister Masuya, if you worry yourself
too much, you'll hurt your health.

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:47.500
You're sure it's going to be all right?

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:50.750
A spy-like spy isn't
always the best solution.

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:03.120
Her name is Hotaru.

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:06.180
I'm thinking we could unleash
her on the village of Mibu.

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:15.040
I'm so sorry!

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:17.230
It wasn't on purpose!

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:21.370
Damn it, that's enough!

00:13:21.370 --> 00:13:23.620
This is the sort of girl she is,

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:26.290
so she'll actually be less
likely to be suspected.

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:28.780
She'd be the best one to send
to feel out the situation.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:31.740
I will do my very best!

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:35.080
Do as you like.

00:13:42.580 --> 00:13:45.160
Miss Hotaru, get the soy sauce for me?

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:46.080
Yes, ma'am.

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:58.830
Excuse me, what does the
gallant Master Okita like?

00:13:58.830 --> 00:14:01.270
You fancy Mr. Okita?

00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:04.320
No, nothing like that...

00:14:06.040 --> 00:14:07.150
You're so mean!

00:14:22.120 --> 00:14:25.800
<i>Oh, I hate this "being a spy" thing.</i>

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:41.730
Are you looking for something, young miss?

00:14:42.870 --> 00:14:44.160
Oh, no...

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:47.030
Which way might the washroom be?

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:50.520
If it's the bathroom,
it's to the back of the yard.

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:53.160
Pardon me.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:56.620
I wonder...

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:02.560
Oh? What's wrong?

00:15:06.040 --> 00:15:07.750
Stop that! It tickles!

00:15:07.750 --> 00:15:10.650
Young miss, what are you doing here?

00:15:15.040 --> 00:15:20.290
I'm Hotaru, and I've been
hired on to help starting today.

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:22.000
Oh, I see.

00:15:25.290 --> 00:15:27.650
Then you must not know your way around.

00:15:28.160 --> 00:15:29.340
I'll give you a tour.

00:15:31.750 --> 00:15:32.700
Yes, please!

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:38.290
This is my room, and back
there is Mr. Kondo's room.

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:41.160
Though he's out today.

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:45.000
Miss Hotaru?

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:45.460
Yes?

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:51.170
When you're taking a tray to Mr. Hijikata,
please make sure to call out a word of warning.

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:54.910
He dislikes people entering silently.

00:15:54.910 --> 00:15:56.180
Gallant Master Okita...

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:05.860
Forgive me.

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:09.070
This is about the only room we have free.

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:13.410
Thank you so much for everything.

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:17.200
I can't very well put you
in with the men, after all.

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:19.410
Please bear with me here for tonight.

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:21.200
Well, then...

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:23.710
I'll do my job properly starting tomorrow.

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:39.770
What is the situation in the capital?

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:43.890
Masuya

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:43.890
Both the watchmen and the Shinsengumi
have increased their numbers.

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:47.960
It seems there is also a spy
assigned to each bridge.

00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:51.410
Is everyone fine?

00:16:51.410 --> 00:16:53.190
Nothing in particular today.

00:17:07.870 --> 00:17:10.300
I can't believe you. You
still haven't learned?

00:17:14.790 --> 00:17:18.510
Shinsengumi boy, are you
in such a rush to die?

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:25.890
And you think you're a spy?
We know everything about you.

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:32.000
Shinsengumi watcher, Susumu Yamazaki.

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:50.880
A spy dancing in the moonlight
can be quite beautiful to behold.

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:57.380
I'd love to have her dancing
in my room next time.

00:17:57.830 --> 00:18:01.040
He wasn't much of an assassin, was he?

00:18:01.040 --> 00:18:03.470
What a spirited boy.

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:09.580
If I hadn't been here, he would be
right over your heads about now.

00:18:09.580 --> 00:18:12.480
Yes, naturally, we're grateful.

00:18:13.290 --> 00:18:16.000
Nothing works better
against spies than spies.

00:18:16.000 --> 00:18:19.370
It would be highly embarrassing
to have them hear me sleep-talking.

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:23.540
Sleep-talking is the least of your worries.
A fire has been lit under your feet.

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:28.210
You know the Mibu ronin are
sniffing about the place, don't you?

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:31.290
They'll be raiding you in no time.

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:33.700
That's where you're wrong.

00:18:33.700 --> 00:18:35.460
They're waiting.

00:18:36.370 --> 00:18:39.450
For me, Toshimaro Yoshida, to make a move.

00:18:39.450 --> 00:18:45.470
That's exactly why I can just sit
here and place my bets in peace.

00:18:45.830 --> 00:18:50.250
A great bet, staking the
fate of the capital.

00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:52.480
You're quite the crazy bastard.

00:18:53.410 --> 00:18:57.580
Well, that's fine. All that
matters to us is the result.

00:18:57.580 --> 00:18:59.700
If it's to defeat the cursed Tokugawa...

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:01.990
We let her talk freely and that woman...

00:19:02.330 --> 00:19:05.990
Leave her be. She's ultimately
nothing but a spy.

00:19:24.040 --> 00:19:25.850
<i>Talk about working hard...</i>

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:54.630
What are you doing?

00:19:55.040 --> 00:19:57.450
What business do you have
in the Commander's room?

00:19:57.450 --> 00:19:58.630
I'm sorry.

00:19:59.250 --> 00:20:03.220
I won't do it again, so please forgive me!

00:20:03.750 --> 00:20:04.950
What are you talking about?

00:20:04.950 --> 00:20:09.770
I began thinking about gallant
Master Okita and then I couldn't sleep.

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:12.770
I thought if I could even get one look
at his face from the next room...

00:20:13.160 --> 00:20:14.580
You know...

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:16.940
Please don't tell Master Okita!

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:18.620
All right, all right.

00:20:18.620 --> 00:20:21.700
If you keep crying here,
you're going to wake everyone up.

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:22.360
Come on.

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:40.360
Ouch!

00:20:58.370 --> 00:21:01.280
Morning, Susumu. I haven't
seen you in three days.

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:10.540
Susumu?

00:21:10.540 --> 00:21:12.580
Masuya

00:21:29.200 --> 00:21:30.350
What are these?!

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:32.350
Hijikata Moron

00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:32.350
What are you trying to pull?!

00:21:33.120 --> 00:21:35.730
I'm so sorry!

00:21:39.580 --> 00:21:42.660
I...

00:21:42.660 --> 00:21:45.240
Would it be all right
if I quit being a spy?

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:48.410
Go ask Yugao about that sort of thing.

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:51.660
I will!

00:22:03.620 --> 00:22:07.910
<i>Gripping the microphone tight,
the hit parade's on parade</i>

00:22:07.910 --> 00:22:11.470
<i>Hey, Jimmy, how you feeling?</i>

00:22:11.470 --> 00:22:15.790
<i>Quite the gentleman when he's off stage</i>

00:22:15.790 --> 00:22:19.480
<i>Hey, Jimmy, a generous spirit too!</i>

00:22:19.480 --> 00:22:23.440
<i>Being such an honest guy,
even his life's plain</i>

00:22:23.440 --> 00:22:27.290
<i>Keep building it up patiently</i>

00:22:27.290 --> 00:22:31.290
<i>May your dreams come true honestly</i>

00:22:31.290 --> 00:22:35.120
<i>Let's go for it again today, Jimmy</i>

